Round 1, read as laid out (6 and 12 PDF pages) by three fictional readers, test instruments: a conference team member with their own agent, a newsroom builder, a first-build finisher. All three got the factory in both editions; all three would start tomorrow from the 3-page edition, only "maybe" from the 10-page one (yes from its draft): the action page comes late and the pages before it read unfinished.

Yours, page by page:
1. Page 1 (03): one line of promise under the subtitle: who it is for, what they will have done by the end (all three).
2. Page 3 (03): the two boxes (words, how to read the scenes) after the first scene, or the glossary cut to the three words the page needs (two of three).
3. Page 11 (10): the action page, the best page for all three, comes after eight pages; move it earlier or point to it from page 3 (the first-build finisher; the conference team member says the same of the team case).
4. Page 8 (10): retitle "the therapy session" to say what happened (the stop at 18:44); the three accounts of the stop in the body, one line each with its date (all three name page 8).
5. Page 10 (10): the several-people factory forward, saying what is shared: one brief, one board, one hold (the conference team member).
6. Page 7 (10): name the claim and the figure the researcher checked (the newsroom builder; also A11).

